  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The velocity vector $v=\u27e8u,v\u27e9$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=\u27e8{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{2t}\u27e9.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82t,\\,2{e}^{2t}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
